oncatError is PyNumber_Add's sequence fallback when neither operand adds: str's, list's and tuple's sq_concat"] [216 1 "// and the bytes-like buffers' refuse b in their own words (nil for any other a)."] [235 1 "// overridesReflected is b's type a proper subtype of a's whose reflected method is its own."] [271 1 "// InPlaceOp is a op= b: the in-place method, else BinaryOp."] [274 17 "// int and float have no in-place methods"] [297 1 "// UnaryOp is +o, -o or ~o."] [308 1 "// RichCompare is a op b (PyObject_RichCompare: the C level's recursion check, then do_richcompare)."] [310 2 "// two exact ints or two exact floats: their own comparison, which recurses into nothing (202b)"] [330 1 "// doRichCompare is do_richcompare: a's method, then b's swapped one, then identity for == and !=."] [360 1 "// Eq is a == b as a Go bool (identity first, as PyObject_RichCompareBool)."] [372 1 "// GetAttr is getattr(o, name)."] [387 1 "// Call is f(*args) with the last len(kwnames) of args keyword arguments."] [396 1 "// GetIter is iter(o)."] [407 1 "// Next is next(it): (nil, nil) at the end."] [416 1 "// GetItem is o[key]."] [418 2 "// an exact list's or tuple's item at an int in range: the slot's answer without its conversions (202b)"] [449 1 "// seqIter is the iterator of a type with __getitem__ and no __iter__ (PY5b: its type registered)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[72 27] [79 27] [129 39] [136 36] [155 49] [166 39] [172 49] [273 39] [276 36] [286 36] [299 34] [313 23] [317 25] [333 30] [339 36] [345 36] [376 32] [398 29] [419 24] [427 28] [437 32] [440 23] [441 41] [475 29]]} (go/file "abstract.go" :imports [

